---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../config/site';

const lastUpdated = 'August 9, 2026';
---

<BaseLayout title="Cookie Policy" description={`Cookie policy for ${SITE.name}.`}>
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-12 sm:px-6">
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-slate-900 dark:text-slate-100">Cookie Policy</h1>
    <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-slate-400">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>

    <div class="prose mt-6 max-w-none dark:prose-invert">
      <h2>What are cookies?</h2>
      <p>
        Cookies (and similar technologies like local storage) are small pieces of data a website can
        store in your browser, usually to remember something between visits — a preference, a login
        session, or in our case, whether you've responded to the cookie banner.
      </p>

      <h2>What Terminal41 uses today</h2>
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Name</th>
            <th>Type</th>
            <th>Purpose</th>
            <th>Duration</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td><code>terminal41-cookie-consent</code></td>
            <td>Local storage (not a cookie)</td>
            <td>Remembers whether you accepted or declined the cookie banner</td>
            <td>Until you clear your browser data</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
      <p>
        That's it — no advertising cookies, no third-party tracking cookies, and no analytics
        cookies are set on {SITE.name} as of the date above.
      </p>

      <h2>What may be added later</h2>
      <p>
        If we add an analytics tool (to see, for example, which airport guides get the most
        traffic), it will only start running for visitors who click "Accept" on the cookie banner —
        visitors who decline, or who haven't made a choice yet, won't have any analytics script
        loaded. When that happens, this table will be updated with the specific cookies that tool
        sets, their provider, and their duration.
      </p>

      <h2>Managing your choice</h2>
      <p>
        You can change your mind at any time by clearing your browser's local storage for this site,
        which will bring the cookie banner back on your next visit. Most browsers also let you block
        or delete cookies and local storage entirely through their privacy settings.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions about this policy can be sent to <a href={`mailto:${SITE.contactEmail}`}>{SITE.contactEmail}</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
